 "why": "Analysed on TWO factors: candidate-set size K and text length. DBpedia is included UNTRUNCATED and supplies the length range (p10 128 -> p90 1300 chars, a 10x spread INSIDE one domain) against clinc/mtop ~34-38 median. Its text-free-picker residual (0.245-0.260) inflates the accuracy LEVEL, but is uncorrelated with text length within the domain (r=-0.089, p=0.21), so the length factor is unconfounded by it. Long texts plus 255 options will truncate some models' context: that is a measurable interaction, not a bug, and truncation must be logged per call. fin-topic excluded (Amendment 1).",
